  "body": "STDO 3.1.0-rc.3 corrects the method and its release-matched companion packages.\n\n- STDO defines its own rules in every tier, including optional profiles.\n- Tracking, needed fact preservation and reconciliation to authoritative workspace truth remain required. A generic register is an optional example; equivalent LLM or other mechanisms are permitted.\n- ODD no longer mandates a downstream runtime, immutable ledger, fixed evaluator API or universal replay architecture. Authority-audit and semantic-judgment guards remain.\n- Product defines the intended end state; Goals hold the current epics. Standards, templates, guides and generated frames agree.\n- Purpose Context and visual artifacts bind the actual RC3 native cut. Skills and the manager have matching release identities.\n\nThe six assets include the native manifest, manager wheel, locked macOS arm64 CPython 3.13 runtime and constraints, companion Product archive and exact cohort record. The cohort records the changed-meaning review, predecessor dispositions, qualification scope and asset identities. Older cuts remain immutable.\n\nThis is a normal published release of an RC cut, consistent with the existing 3.1 line. Construction remains on STDO 3.0.4. Publication does not adopt RC3 for existing consumers or change global installations. Coverage is limited to the recorded subjects; whole-method qualification, automatic host pickup, wider effectiveness and human exact-cut acceptance are separate.\n"
